        "labelColor": "black",
        "color": "light-blue",
        "fill": "solid",
        "size": "m",
        "font": "sans",
        "align": "middle",
        "verticalAlign": "middle",
        "richText": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Pair construction and smoothing\nExample: w0 [0.0,0.4] + w1 [0.4,0.9] -> \"w0 w1\" [0.0,0.9]\nRaw groups preserve first start and second end, then smoothing defines total span = [firstPair.Start,lastPair.End].\nScale pair durations so their sum equals that span. Set minEffective = min(300 ms, span/pairCount). For each short pair, borrow only from later pairs without reducing them below minEffective. Rebuild all pair ranges contiguously; force final end to original final end.\nResult: readable, gap-free pair display; not a literal copy of raw word gaps." }] }]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "shape:repeat-detail",
      "typeName": "shape",
      "type": "geo",
      "x": 2740,
      "y": 1170,
      "rotation": 0,
      "index": "adPzw",
      "parentId": "page:page",
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "props": {
        "geo": "rectangle",
        "dash": "solid",
        "url": "",
        "w": 1100,
        "h": 370,
        "growY": 0,
        "scale": 1,
        "flipX": false,
        "flipY": false,
        "labelColor": "black",
        "color": "yellow",
        "fill": "solid",
        "size": "m",
        "font": "sans",
        "align": "middle",
        "verticalAlign": "middle",
        "richText": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Repeat segment matcher\nFor segment tokens vs candidate ayah tokens, local alignment awards +2 for exact normalized match and -1 for a gap/mismatch; non-positive cells reset to zero. It keeps only current and previous DP rows.\nAccept when valid and NOT (matches < minMatches AND coverage < 20%). minMatches is 1 for <4 segment tokens, otherwise 2.\nChoose current or next ayah by matches, coverage, score, then span length. The cursor only moves forward. Partial canonical phrase clears translation." }] }]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "shape:pause-detail",
      "typeName": "shape",
      "type": "geo",
      "x": 120,
      "y": 1170,
      "rotation": 0,
      "index": "aeNrE",
      "parentId": "page:page",
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "props": {
        "geo": "rectangle",
        "dash": "solid",
        "url": "",
        "w": 1050,
        "h": 370,
        "growY": 0,
        "scale": 1,
        "flipX": false,
        "flipY": false,
        "labelColor": "black",
        "color": "light-green",
        "fill": "solid",
        "size": "m",
        "font": "sans",
        "align": "middle",
        "verticalAlign": "middle",
        "richText": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Sequential pause-sensitive branch\nFFmpeg silencedetect uses pause_db (default -35 dB) and pause_sec (default 0.2 s).\nWith word timing: locate the last word ending before silence, reject splits that leave a one-visible-letter side, construct fragments from first/last word times, then merge tiny text and <120 ms fragments.\nWithout word timing: subtract silence intervals, allocate canonical words by speech-fragment duration.\nThe final fragments intentionally have no WordTimings: they are sequential speech chunks." }] }]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "shape:timing-example",
      "typeName": "shape",
      "type": "geo",
      "x": 4070,
      "y": 1170,
      "rotation": 0,
      "index": "afMmX",
      "parentId": "page:page",
      "isLocked": false,
      "opacity": 1,
      "meta": {},
      "props": {
        "geo": "rectangle",
        "dash": "solid",
        "url": "",
        "w": 840,
        "h": 370,
        "growY": 0,
        "scale": 1,
        "flipX": false,
        "flipY": false,
        "labelColor": "black",
        "color": "grey",
        "fill": "solid",
        "size": "m",
        "font": "sans",
        "align": "middle",
        "verticalAlign": "middle",
        "richText": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [{ "type": "paragraph", "content": [{ "type": "text", "text": "Timing repair sequence\n1. Apply optional global word offset, clamped to current ayah range.\n2. Replace outer ayah bounds with first and last word endpoints.\n3. Merge standalone marks and enforce monotonic, >=100 ms words. An extended word can extend its ayah end.\n4. Repair a suspiciously compressed non-final ayah by evenly filling the reliable interval before next ayah.\nThis order protects full-audio timestamps before provisional bounds can clamp them." }] }]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "shape:caveats",
      "typeName": "shape",
      "type": "geo",
      "x": 5080,
      "y": 1170,
      "rotation": 0,
      "index": "agoUH",
      "parentId": "page:page",
